'''Eric Ambrose Gordon Jr.''' (born December 25, 1988)<ref>{{cite web|title=Eric Gordon Stats|url=https://www.basketball-reference.com/players/g/gordoer01.html|website=Basketball-Reference.com|access-date=November 8, 2020}}</ref> is a Bahamian-American professional [[basketball]] player who last played for the [[Philadelphia 76ers]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). In high school, he was named [[Indiana Mr. Basketball]] during his senior year while playing at [[North Central High School (Indianapolis)|North Central High School]]. He is known, in part, as the subject of a recruiting competition between the [[University of Illinois at Urbana–Champaign|University of Illinois]] and [[Indiana University Bloomington|Indiana University]] in the spring and summer of 2006; because of Gordon's talent and high level of play that year, his recruitment was the subject of media coverage.

Gordon played one season of [[college basketball]] at Indiana<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.indystar.com/apps/pbcs.dll/article?AID=/20061108/SPORTS0601/61108017|title=Gordon seals IU deal with signing}}</ref> and was considered one of the top collegiate players in the nation that year.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20070113004213/http://www.cstv.com/hoopsodyssey/2007/01/08/ Eric Gordon: Before the Storm]</ref> He finished his freshman season leading the [[Big Ten]] in scoring and tied for 19th in the nation at 21.5 points per game.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/stats/player?season=2008 |access-date=April 21, 2023 |title=NCAA College Basketball Statistics: 2007–2008 Men's Basketball Leaders – Points}}</ref> Gordon entered the [[2008 NBA draft]] and was selected seventh overall by the [[Los Angeles Clippers]].

